WEBVTT

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.750
When several agents must coordinate,

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.671
there is rarely one right answer.

00:00:05.101 --> 00:00:07.971
Here, each agent has two valid landmarks.

00:00:08.321 --> 00:00:10.132
Averaging between them leads nowhere.

00:00:11.535 --> 00:00:14.115
Offline multi-agent RL increasingly trains

00:00:14.135 --> 00:00:15.956
a centralized generative teacher

00:00:15.976 --> 00:00:18.396
over joint actions, then distills it

00:00:18.416 --> 00:00:20.286
into fast, one-step students

00:00:20.396 --> 00:00:22.427
that act on local information only.

00:00:23.803 --> 00:00:25.585
Two cars must pass a rock

00:00:25.605 --> 00:00:26.896
from opposite sides.

00:00:27.507 --> 00:00:28.798
Each car, on its own,

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:30.460
can go above or below.

00:00:31.171 --> 00:00:33.062
But only the pair decides:

00:00:33.713 --> 00:00:35.064
opposite sides get through,

00:00:35.595 --> 00:00:37.346
the same side collides.

00:00:38.318 --> 00:00:40.760
The valid pairs, weighted by how often

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:41.831
they appear in the data,

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:43.733
form the mode support.

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:47.017
The problem starts in the teacher.

00:00:47.708 --> 00:00:49.950
Standard flow matching pairs noise

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:51.321
with targets at random,

00:00:51.591 --> 00:00:53.473
so nearby noise samples are pulled

00:00:53.493 --> 00:00:55.245
toward different coordination modes.

00:00:55.876 --> 00:00:58.208
The teacher leaves mass between modes.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.400
And because distillation regresses

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.432
each student onto a conditional mean,

00:01:02.842 --> 00:01:04.393
that error is not absorbed.

00:01:04.644 --> 00:01:05.595
It is inherited.

00:01:07.002 --> 00:01:08.724
MoSDOT fixes the assignment

00:01:08.744 --> 00:01:09.815
before training.

00:01:10.305 --> 00:01:11.786
It summarizes the replay

00:01:11.806 --> 00:01:13.588
into a finite mode support

00:01:13.608 --> 00:01:16.260
with capacities, then solves a conditional

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:18.742
semi-discrete optimal transport problem.

00:01:19.353 --> 00:01:21.485
Noise space is split into cells,

00:01:21.755 --> 00:01:23.086
one per joint mode,

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.668
each holding exactly its share of mass.

00:01:26.239 --> 00:01:28.081
The teacher then learns clean routes

00:01:28.101 --> 00:01:29.432
from noise to modes.

00:01:30.828 --> 00:01:33.262
The cleaner routing survives distillation.

00:01:33.753 --> 00:01:36.037
MoSDOT students keep 97%

00:01:36.057 --> 00:01:37.990
of their actions on valid modes,

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:41.365
while baseline students leave 15 to 64%

00:01:41.385 --> 00:01:42.918
of theirs between modes.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.794
Some coordination cannot be represented

00:01:46.814 --> 00:01:48.606
by independent agents at all,

00:01:48.957 --> 00:01:50.388
like this XOR task.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.824
A shared random signal lets agents agree

00:01:53.844 --> 00:01:55.616
on a mode without communicating,

00:01:55.886 --> 00:01:58.280
which isolates this strict-product gap.

00:01:59.698 --> 00:02:02.152
On offline multi-agent benchmarks,

00:02:02.523 --> 00:02:03.985
MoSDOT is competitive

00:02:04.005 --> 00:02:06.099
with strong generative baselines,

00:02:06.409 --> 00:02:08.193
with the clearest gains when the data

00:02:08.213 --> 00:02:10.446
contains diverse joint behavior.

00:02:11.858 --> 00:02:13.800
Multi-Agent Coordination via

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:15.673
Support-Preserving Distillation.
